  "name": "Nova Cançó (Els Setze Jutges movement)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Catalan-language song movement launched in Barcelona in 1961 by the Els Setze Jutges collective around Miquel Porter, Josep Maria Espinàs and Delfí Abella, modelled on French chanson rive gauche and radicalized by Raimon's 'Al vent' (1963) — solo voice with nylon-string guitar or piano, later widened to string and wind arrangements, setting Catalan and Valencian poetry (Espriu, Estellés) in strophic through-built forms with declamatory, non-vibrato delivery and slow crescendo builds toward anthemic refrains.",
